KickOS full-C++ opt-in test
PASS: app constructors ran in main's thread
PASS: app statics in the app image's window
PASS: two threads' first throws at once are both caught
PASS: exception caught by exact type
PASS: exception caught by std::exception base
PASS: stack unwind runs local dtors
PASS: std::vector<int> push_back + sum == 5050
PASS: std::string concat == KickOS/full-c++
PASS: virtual dispatch picks override
PASS: dynamic_cast to real type succeeds
PASS: dynamic_cast to wrong type yields nullptr
PASS: typeid reflects dynamic type
PASS: getentropy refuses with ENOSYS
PASS: random_device refuses to construct with no source
PASS: a static two threads reach at once is built once
PASS: a contended call_once runs once and every caller sees its effect
PASS: a call_once whose function threw runs again, then never
PASS: a shared_ptr two threads copy and drop keeps its count
PASS: two std::threads take turns over a condition variable
PASS: a timed condition wait ends at its deadline
PASS: a timed lock of a held mutex ends at its deadline
PASS: a recursive timed lock waits until every level is released
PASS: a recursive wait held two deep gives both levels back
PASS: a std::thread runs at its creator's priority
PASS: a thread inheriting its priority ignores the one it names
PASS: each thread rethrows its own caught exception while another holds one
PASS: each thread counts only its own uncaught exception
PASS: a deleted key's index serves a new key
PASS: a value a deleted key left behind is never the new key's
PASS: a thread a non-creator joined has its slot free again
PASS: a join returns for a thread that ended by kos_exit
PASS: a join returns for a thread its creator cancelled
PASS: a new thread's thread_locals start zeroed and are built for it
PASS: a thread_local destructor a key destructor registers runs
PASS: a detached thread that starts and detaches threads keeps its own record
PASS: a detached thread that returned leaves no record behind
PASS: hardware_concurrency counts the task's cores
